{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "0b1t5phe-c0re-4a11-9e00-5c4001c0113c",
    "name": "Orbit Sphere \u2014 API",
    "description": "Write API for the Orbit Sphere school platform.\n\n**Built so far: 1 of 28 planned write endpoints.** The plan for the rest is in\n`backend/src/main/java/com/orbitastra/backend/controllers/core/README.md`.\n\nRun the folder top to bottom: request 01 saves `schoolId` and `createdSubdomain`, which request 05 needs.\n\nEvery request carries tests, so **Run collection** is a regression suite, not just a list of calls.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Core / School",
      "description": "Tenant provisioning. Platform surface \u2014 no school session exists yet, because provisioning is what creates the school these requests are about.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 Create school \u2014 full payload",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a schoolId', () => pm.expect(body.schoolId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('starts at PROVISIONING', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('PROVISIONING'));",
                  "pm.test('Location header points at the new school', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql('/platform/schools/' + body.schoolId));",
                  "pm.test('subdomain was normalised to lowercase', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(body.subdomain).to.eql(body.subdomain.toLowerCase()));",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('schoolId', body.schoolId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('createdSubdomain', body.subdomain);",
                  "console.log('created ' + body.subdomain + ' -> ' + body.schoolId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Orbit Astra International School\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Rohan Shinde\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"orbit-astra-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"+919876543210\",\n  \"emailAddress\": \"admin@orbit-school.edu\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\",\n  \"addressLine\": \"12, MG Road\",\n  \"city\": \"Pune\",\n  \"stateOrProvince\": \"Maharashtra\",\n  \"postalCode\": \"411001\",\n  \"trial\": false\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every field the request accepts. Saves schoolId and subdomain as collection variables so later requests can reuse them.\n\nsubdomain uses {{$timestamp}} because it is GLOBALLY unique, not per-school \u2014 a fixed value only works once and then returns 409 forever."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "02 Create school \u2014 minimum payload",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('optional fields left out is fine', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().schoolId).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Minimum Fields School\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"minimum-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only the six required fields. Everything else is optional and stored as null."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "03 Create school \u2014 trial tenant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('status is TRIAL', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('TRIAL'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Trial School\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"trial-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\",\n  \"trial\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "trial:true starts the tenant at TRIAL instead of PROVISIONING. Both are legal starting states; ACTIVE is not, and the request cannot ask for it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "04 Subdomain is normalised before it is stored",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const s = pm.response.json().subdomain;",
                  "pm.test('trimmed, lowercased, hyphenated', () => pm.expect(s).to.match(/^norm-check-\\d+$/));",
                  "pm.test('no spaces or underscores survive', () => pm.expect(s).to.not.match(/[\\s_]/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Normalisation Check\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"  Norm_Check {{$timestamp}}  \",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sends '  Orbit_Astra School {{$timestamp}}  '. Whitespace is trimmed, case lowered, spaces and underscores become hyphens.\n\nThe subdomain in the RESPONSE is the one to use afterwards \u2014 not the one you sent."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "05 Duplicate subdomain \u2192 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('code is SUBDOMAIN_TAKEN', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('SUBDOMAIN_TAKEN'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Duplicate Attempt\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"{{createdSubdomain}}\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reuses the subdomain saved by request 01. Run 01 first.\n\n409 and not 400: the request is perfectly well formed. Somebody else simply has that name."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "06 Reserved subdomain \u2192 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('code is SUBDOMAIN_RESERVED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('SUBDOMAIN_RESERVED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Reserved Attempt\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"api\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "'api' is on the platform's reserved list. So are www, admin, login, auth, cdn, mail and about thirty more.\n\nThis is not a naming preference: a school owning 'login' would receive credentials meant for the platform."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "07 Malformed subdomain \u2192 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('code is SUBDOMAIN_INVALID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('SUBDOMAIN_INVALID'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Bad Shape\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"-bad-\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Leading and trailing hyphens are not a valid DNS label."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "08 Unknown time zone \u2192 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('code is TIME_ZONE_INVALID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('TIME_ZONE_INVALID'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"Bad Zone\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ankit Kumar\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"bad-zone-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Pune\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"IN\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "'Asia/Pune' looks reasonable and does not exist. Checked against the JVM's IANA zone set, which no regex or annotation can do.\n\nThis matters more than it looks: defaultTimeZone decides which calendar date an attendance record falls on, so a wrong value is wrong everywhere at once."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "09 Missing and invalid fields \u2192 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('code is VALIDATION_FAILED', () => pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('VALIDATION_FAILED'));",
                  "pm.test('errors are keyed by field', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fieldErrors).to.have.property('schoolName');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fieldErrors).to.have.property('accountHolderName');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fieldErrors).to.have.property('countryCode');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.fieldErrors).to.have.property('emailAddress');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schoolName\": \"\",\n  \"subdomain\": \"validation-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"ZZZ\",\n  \"emailAddress\": \"not-an-email\",\n  \"defaultLocale\": \"en-IN\",\n  \"defaultTimeZone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Blank name, no account holder, a three-letter country code.\n\n400 with per-field messages, because these are caught by Jakarta annotations on the request record before the controller method is entered."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "10 Malformed JSON \u2192 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('code is MALFORMED_REQUEST', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('MALFORMED_REQUEST'));",
                  "pm.test('no stack trace leaks', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('org.springframework'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"schoolName\": }",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/platform/schools",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "platform",
                "schools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Deliberately broken body.\n\nAsserts the response carries no stack trace \u2014 devtools enables those by default, and they hand over package names and framework versions to anyone who can send a bad request."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3456",
      "description": "server.port is 3456, set in application.properties."
    },
    {
      "key": "schoolId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by request 01."
    },
    {
      "key": "createdSubdomain",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by request 01, used by 05."
    }
  ]
}
